description: Hard bans for every project using this pack (any AI)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Restrictions

## Never

- Treat **install** as file-copy only — must **ask + fill** Profile in the same session
- Skip **project intake** when Project Profile fields are `TBD`
- Keep intake answers only in chat without writing them to `CURSOR.md` / settings / skill / `concept-domain.mdc`
- Start feature work while required Profile fields are still `TBD` (unless user deferred a field)
- **Remove or weaken default rules**: forms, custom UI styling (Tailwind base), validation, PHP migrate/seed, icons-states
- Replace locked Tailwind UI system with another framework or per-page one-off skins
- **Mix implementation phases** or skip `/phase-exit` gates
- Invent DB schema or domain rules that ignore the stated **concept**
- Commit secrets, API keys, or filled `.env` files
- Hardcode production API hosts, FTP, or DB credentials in source
- Add a new env key used in production without adding the same key to **GitHub Secrets**
- Deploy to production/live with secrets only on a local `.env` and not in GitHub Secrets
- Add `.sql` migrations or seeds — use PHP `migration` / `seed` only
- Concatenate user input into SQL (SQL injection)
- Return HTTP `200` with an error-only payload when a proper error status exists
- Rely on UI hiding for authorization — enforce roles server-side
- Hard-delete user-facing records when soft delete (`deleted_at`) is the project norm
- Mix bare native form controls with the unified custom form system
- Mix Bootstrap/MUI/default third-party theme with the locked Tailwind product skin
- Invent a second visual language when a UI baseline is defined
- Skip shared **404 / status-error / empty** screens, **skeleton loaders**, or **lazy load**
- Replace the locked icon system without updating Profile (Material Icons **or** Lottie web)
- Enable SEO without Schema.org JSON-LD when Project Profile SEO = `on`
- Copy third-party product brands, trademarks, or marketing copy into the project
- Copy a reference wholesale — take only the parts needed for the requested work
- Write where a design or pattern came from inside files (code, comments, docs, commits, UI copy)
- Run destructive git/db commands without explicit user confirmation
- When Layout strategy = `layout`: use fluid-only stretched layouts instead of distinct mobile · tablet · desktop layouts
- When Clients = **web + mobile**: split into separate mobile and web projects/repos when Profile requires a **single codebase**
- Skip asking the Layout strategy choice (`normal` \| `layout` \| `auto`), or ignore the recorded choice
- Build P2 screens before `route-layouts.mdc` is filled and approved
- Require the dev to hand over hex codes/fonts — the AI proposes the design; dev approves
- Ship harsh or manipulative design (pure black on pure white, big saturated fills, dark patterns)
- Assume a single AI/tool, keep decisions only in chat, or skip the AI Handoff Log

## Prefer

- Edit existing files over creating parallel structures
- Shared UI components and design tokens
- Prepared statements / parameterized queries
- Documented env in `.env.example` only (keys + placeholders — never live values)
- Production/live values in **GitHub Secrets**: FTP/SSH, database, `APP_URL` / API hosts (web **and** mobile when split), and every new env key — CI injects at deploy (`/deploy`)
- Concept → domain file → migrations → API → UI
- Layout = `layout`: one project, distinct per-class layouts; shared tokens/forms/components across surfaces
- Layout = `normal`: mobile-first reflow of one composition
- Build from `route-layouts.mdc`; edit it first when a layout changes
